<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Find percentiles from frequency table</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>
Find \(P_{@p1@}\) and \(P_{@p2@}\) for the following frequency distribution, where
\(P_n\) denotes the \(n^{th}\) percentile.
</p>

<p>
First complete the cumulative frequency column.
</p>

<table border="solid">
  <tr>
    <th width="30%" style="text-align:center">Value</th>
    <th width="30%" style="text-align:center">Frequency</th>
    <th width="40%" style="text-align:center">Cumulative frequency</th>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@x1@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@f1@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@cf1@}\)</td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@x2@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@f2@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@x3@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@f3@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@x4@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@f4@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@x5@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@f5@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@x6@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@f6@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">[[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p>
Using the completed cumulative frequency distribution, find:
</p>

<p>
\(P_{@p1@}=\) [[input:ans6]] [[validation:ans6]] [[feedback:prt6]]
</p>

<p>
\(P_{@p2@}=\) [[input:ans7]] [[validation:ans7]] [[feedback:prt7]]
</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h4>Worked solution</h4>

<p>
First calculate the cumulative frequencies by successively adding the frequencies:
</p>

<table border="solid">
  <tr>
    <th width="30%" style="text-align:center">Value</th>
    <th width="30%" style="text-align:center">Frequency</th>
    <th width="40%" style="text-align:center">Cumulative frequency</th>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@x1@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@f1@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@cf1@}\)</td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@x2@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@f2@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@cf2@}\)</td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@x3@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@f3@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@cf3@}\)</td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@x4@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@f4@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@cf4@}\)</td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@x5@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@f5@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@cf5@}\)</td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@x6@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@f6@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@cf6@}\)</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p>
There are \(N={@N@}\) observations in total.
</p>

<hr>

<p>
The position of \(P_{@p1@}\) is
</p>

[[if test="intpos1"]]

<p>
\[
\frac{@p1@}{100}\times {@N@}
= {@ppos1@}.
\]
</p>

<p>
Therefore, \(P_{@p1@}\) corresponds to the
\({@ppos1@}^{\text{th}}\) observation.
</p>

<p>
From the cumulative frequencies, this observation has the value
\({@ta6@}\). Therefore,
</p>

[[else]]

<p>
\[
\frac{@p1@}{100}\times {@N@}
= {@dispdp(ppos1,2)@}.
\]
</p>

<p>
Therefore, \(P_{@p1@}\) lies between the
\({@lowerpos1@}^{\text{th}}\) and
\({@upperpos1@}^{\text{th}}\) observations.
</p>

<p>
From the cumulative frequencies, both of these observations have the value
\({@ta6@}\). Therefore,
</p>

[[/if]]

<p>
\[
\boxed{P_{@p1@}={@ta6@}}.
\]
</p>

<hr>

<p>
The position of \(P_{@p2@}\) is
</p>

[[if test="intpos2"]]

<p>
\[
\frac{@p2@}{100}\times {@N@}
= {@ppos2@}.
\]
</p>

<p>
Therefore, \(P_{@p2@}\) corresponds to the
\({@ppos2@}^{\text{th}}\) observation.
</p>

<p>
From the cumulative frequencies, this observation has the value
\({@ta7@}\). Therefore,
</p>

[[else]]

<p>
\[
\frac{@p2@}{100}\times {@N@}
= {@dispdp(ppos2,2)@}.
\]
</p>

<p>
Therefore, \(P_{@p2@}\) lies between the
\({@lowerpos2@}^{\text{th}}\) and
\({@upperpos2@}^{\text{th}}\) observations.
</p>

<p>
From the cumulative frequencies, both of these observations have the value
\({@ta7@}\). Therefore,
</p>

[[/if]]

<p>
\[
\boxed{P_{@p2@}={@ta7@}}.
\]
</p>]]></text>
